// Chronicle Release Opcodes Demo
// This script demonstrates the new opcodes introduced in the Chronicle release.
//
// To test version-dependent behavior, go to Settings and set Transaction Version.
// Version 1: Standard rules (default)
// Version 2+: Chronicle rules (relaxed malleability restrictions)
//
// NOTE: String data in Bitcoin Script is represented as hex values.
// Use the Tools panel (Tools button in toolbar) to convert text to hex.

// =====================================================
// 1. Transaction Version Opcode (ver)
// =====================================================
// Push the current transaction version onto the stack

ver
dup
// Stack now has: [version, version]

// =====================================================
// 2. Version-based Conditional (verIf)
// =====================================================
// Execute block if transaction version >= comparison value

2 verIf
  // This block executes if version >= 2 (Chronicle mode)
  drop  // Drop duplicate version
  1     // Push 1 to indicate Chronicle mode
else
  // This block executes if version < 2 (Standard mode)
  drop  // Drop duplicate version
  0     // Push 0 to indicate Standard mode
endIf

// Store the mode indicator
toAltStack

// =====================================================
// 3. String Operations: subStr, left, right
// =====================================================
// NOTE: All string data is hex-encoded

// "BSV Blockchain" = 42535620426c6f636b636861696e (hex)
// subStr - Extract substring by start index and length
// Stack: [string, start_index, length] -> [substring]
42535620426c6f636b636861696e 8 10 subStr
// Result: 426c6f636b ("Block" - hex chars at positions 8-17)

// Verify we got "Block" (426c6f636b)
426c6f636b equal verify

// "Bitcoin" = 426974636f696e (hex)
// left - Get leftmost n characters
426974636f696e 6 left
// Result: 426974 ("Bit" = 6 hex chars)
// Note: 426974 is all digits, so use 0x prefix to force hex interpretation
0x426974 equal verify

// right - Get rightmost n characters
426974636f696e 8 right
// Result: 636f696e ("coin" = 8 hex chars)
636f696e equal verify

// =====================================================
// 4. Arithmetic: 2mul, 2div
// =====================================================

// 2mul - Multiply by 2
10 2mul
// Result: 20
20 equal verify

// 2div - Divide by 2 (floor division)
15 2div
// Result: 7 (floor of 7.5)
7 equal verify

// =====================================================
// 5. Numerical Shift: lShiftNum, rShiftNum
// =====================================================
// These preserve sign, unlike bitwise lShift/rShift

// lShiftNum - Left shift preserving sign
8 2 lShiftNum
// Result: 32 (8 << 2 = 8 * 4)
32 equal verify

// rShiftNum - Right shift preserving sign
32 3 rShiftNum
// Result: 4 (32 >> 3 = 32 / 8)
4 equal verify

// Test sign preservation with negative numbers
-16 1 rShiftNum
// Result: -8 (sign preserved)
-8 equal verify

// =====================================================
// 6. verNotIf Example
// =====================================================
// Execute block if transaction version < comparison value

ver
2 verNotIf
  // This executes if version < 2 (NOT Chronicle)
  1  // Standard mode indicator
else
  // This executes if version >= 2 (Chronicle mode)
  2  // Chronicle mode indicator
endIf

// Clean up and verify
drop

// Retrieve mode indicator from alt stack
fromAltStack

// =====================================================
// Final Result
// =====================================================
// Stack should contain: mode indicator (0 for standard, 1 for Chronicle)
// The script completes successfully if all verifications pass

// Verify we have a valid result
dup 0notEqual
// Success! Script execution complete.
